1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Listen to a presentation on the five most frequently visited museums of Australia.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Now listen to the first part of the talk and answer questions 11 to 15.

4
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Good evening and thank you Mr. Livingstone for inviting me to speak before you all.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
To all of you, thank you for being here.

6
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
As you know, my name is Dr. Harold Kramer.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
I'm the Chief of Operations for the Pacific Museum of Natural History located here in Queensland.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
I will be discussing the five most frequently visited museums of Australia.

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,000
As you all know, a museum is an institution that houses and showcases collections of artifacts and relics

10
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,000
which are of scientific, artistic, cultural, or historic value and make valuable displays and presentations.

11
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Not only that, museums are places that provide facilities for study,

12
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
whether it's in the realm of science, history, aesthetics, or a combination of all three.

13
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,000
The artifacts, models, displays, and other presentations are open for viewing by people through exhibitions.

14
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
It is a general notion that museums are visited only by scholars or students.

15
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
This notion is unfortunate and archaic because it springs from the misconception that museums are dreary and drab places.

16
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,000
On the contrary, museums can be quite fascinating and intriguing places.

17
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
I think you'll be very much surprised to learn how many people visit these institutions annually.

18
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Among these visitors, you will of course find scholars, students, and tourists.

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
But you will find many, many other people who visit.

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Often, you'll find whole families showing up at a museum with the parents explaining that they bring their children

21
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
to learn about the world around them or about things from the past.

22
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Others come because by visiting, they learn about new things and have great, fun-filled experiences.

23
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
It really is a pleasure to see all these people visit.

24
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
It makes the job of working in a museum very fulfilling.

25
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20.

26
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20.

27
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Tonight, I'm going to tell you about the top five museums of Australia.

28
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:38,000
The museums that I'm going to speak about are the National Museum of Australia, Museum of Contemporary Art,

29
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Australian National Maritime Museum, National Sports Museum, and the National Gallery.

30
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:51,000
After I describe these museums, I will reveal how many have visited them during the summer months this year.

31
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
The number will astound you.

32
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
We'll begin with the National Museum.

33
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
It was established in 1980 and officially opened in Canberra.

34
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:07,000
It preserves the social history of the Aborigines and traces the events that have shaped the nation through the ages.

35
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,000
It houses the world's largest collection of Aboriginal bark paintings and stone tools

36
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:17,000
and is a delight to archaeologists and those interested in Aboriginal culture.

37
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:24,000
The Museum of Contemporary Art was founded in 1996 and was created as a permanent institution for contemporary art.

38
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
It is located in Sydney and is evolving in exhibiting, interpreting, and collecting contemporary art

39
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
from all over Australia and the world.

40
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
It is a hub for lovers of modern art.

41
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
The Australian National Maritime Museum is located in Sydney

42
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
and is visited for its display of ships and submarines that are often docked in the harbour in front of the museum.

43
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
It allows visitors to go aboard these vessels and experience life at sea.

44
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,000
It also displays items relating to Australia's dependence on the oceans

45
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,000
and has been open to the public since 1973.

46
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:02,000
The National Sports Museum is an amazing museum inside the Melbourne Cricket Grounds.

47
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:09,000
As the name suggests, it keeps a record of the sporting stories from its early beginnings to present times.

48
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Sporting heroes, their achievements, and other memorable sporting moments find a place here.

49
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:19,000
It was founded in 1969 and includes the Australian Cricket Hall of Fame,

50
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:24,000
the Australian Racing Museum, and the Sport Australia Hall of Fame.

51
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:29,000
It also features a large interactive area that is popular with all ages.

52
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:35,000
The National Gallery, located in Perth, is by far the most famous gallery in all of Australia.

53
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:41,000
It has extensive displays of western art, beginning from medieval times and stretching to modern art.

54
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:46,000
It also features eastern art, mostly in the form of traditional art from South and East Asia,

55
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
as well as international modern art.

56
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Over the one century of its existence, it has collected and displayed sculptures, paintings, murals, relics, and lots more.

57
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Over the summer this year, these museums witnessed record numbers of visitors.

58
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,000
The National Museum alone received 10,000 visitors.

59
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:12,000
That is the end of part 2. You now have half a minute to check your answers.

60
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Now turn to part 3.
